Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 23:20:01 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 37/52] kernel: sync primitive info sizes fix and LW mutex
 owner UID (#4273)

* kernel: leave the whole struct's size in the info calls' size field

The info calls wrote back the size the game asked for.
Vita writes the size of the whole struct there, whatever part of it the game asked for.

* kernel: take any rwlock info size up to the struct, like the other info calls

The rwlock info refused every size below the whole struct and took any size above it.
Vita takes any size up to the struct and refuses a bigger one with NO_MEMORY, like the other info calls.

* kernel: implement the lightweight condition variable info

* kernel: keep a mutex owner and a rwlock writer as their thread's UID

A LW  mutex stays locked by an owner that ended, even once it was deleted, and its info keeps reporting that UID.
The mutex kept a reference to the owner's thread for it, so a deleted thread's stack, TLS and CPU state stayed allocated until the mutex went away.

(cherry picked from commit 7622d0fbbdfadea9cb0cc44458d570fc201a438a)
